---
import ProfileLinks from "../components/ProfileLinks.astro";
import { automateUrl } from "../data/profiles";
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import "../interior.css";
---

<Layout
  title="Founder"
  description="Explore Vishwa Vigyan with founder Souvik Ghosh. Try a QuoteDesk demo, see the AI development portfolio or bring a physics problem to VV Research Desk."
>
  <article class="folio work">
    <header class="profile-opening">
      <div class="opening-copy">
        <span class="stamp">Souvik Ghosh / Business</span>
        <h1>Founder</h1>
        <p class="intro">
          I founded <a href="https://vishwavigyan.com/">Vishwa Vigyan</a>.
          Sometimes the problem on my desk is a physicist’s simulation that
          gives the wrong answer. Sometimes it’s a trader spending the evening
          typing prices into quotations.
        </p>
        <div class="profile-actions">
          <a
            class="profile-button"
            href="https://vishwavigyan.com/contact.html"
          >
            Bring me a project
          </a>
          <a href="#building">Explore the work ↓</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="quote-sample">
        <span class="folio-meta">VV Automate / Product example</span>
        <h2>From enquiry to quotation</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>A buyer sends a list on WhatsApp.</li>
          <li>QuoteDesk matches items to the seller’s price list.</li>
          <li>The seller checks the PDF and sends it.</li>
        </ol>
        <a href="https://automate.vishwavigyan.com/sample-quotation.pdf">
          Open a sample quotation · PDF
        </a>
      </div>
    </header>
    <section class="folio-row" id="building">
      <div>
        <span class="stamp">AI development</span>
        <h2>Inside VV Automate</h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>
          I build tools around jobs a business already does. Start with the
          QuoteDesk demo. The other product pages show how a system can be set
          up for your business.
        </p>
        <dl class="product-index">
          <dt>
            <a href="https://automate.vishwavigyan.com/quotedesk/#demo">
              QuoteDesk · see the demo
            </a>
          </dt>
          <dd>
            Turn a typed enquiry or a photographed list into a quotation ready
            for review.
          </dd>
          <dt>
            <a href="https://automate.vishwavigyan.com/billdrop/">BillDrop</a>
          </dt>
          <dd>
            Read a supplier’s bill and prepare an entry for checking before it
            reaches Tally.
          </dd>
          <dt>
            <a href="https://automate.vishwavigyan.com/tradedocs/">TradeDocs</a>
          </dt>
          <dd>
            Prepare a packing list and an invoice from the same shipment
            details, then estimate the cost per unit.
          </dd>
          <dt>
            <a href="https://automate.vishwavigyan.com/get-found/">Get Found</a>
          </dt>
          <dd>
            Put the right business details in the places where local customers
            search.
          </dd>
          <dt>
            <a href="https://automate.vishwavigyan.com/custom-systems/">
              Custom Systems
            </a>
          </dt>
          <dd>
            Start with a repeating job, its documents and the decisions that
            still need a person.
          </dd>
        </dl>
        <a class="profile-button" href={automateUrl}>
          Explore the full VV Automate portfolio
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="folio-row">
      <div>
        <span class="stamp">Scientific computing</span>
        <h2>VV Research Desk</h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>
          A simulation can run without errors and still give an impossible
          result. One worked example at the Desk uses a transport calculation
          with a missing coupling. Another starts with a noisy frequency sweep
          and shows how to extract the resonance and its width.
        </p>
        <p>
          The examples use synthetic data. For your own project, bring the plot,
          code or fit and the point where it stopped making sense.
        </p>
        <a href="https://research.vishwavigyan.com/">
          See the worked examples at VV Research Desk →
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="folio-row">
      <h2>Where the ventures fit</h2>
      <div>
        <p>
          Vishwa Vigyan grew out of{" "}
          <a href="https://masterwithin.net/">Master Within</a> and Sree Sree
          Thakur Anukulchandra’s vision of the Satsang Vishwa Vigyan Kendra. Its
          other business lines are VV Deep-Tech Studio, VV Trade, VV Learning
          and VV Media Lab.
        </p>
        <p id="instruments">
          My <a href="/inventor/">inventor profile</a> documents the rooftop
          telescope.
        </p>
        <p id="renatus">
          My <a href="/wellness-rd/">Renatus Wellness profile</a> covers
          equipment development and sourcing.
        </p>
        <p id="spirit">
          My <a href="/spiritual-mentor/">spiritual mentor profile</a>{" "}
          introduces the foundation behind the work.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <ProfileLinks related={["apps", "wellness-rd", "inventor"]} />
  </article>
</Layout>
<style>
  .quote-sample {
    padding: clamp(20px, 3vw, 34px);
    background: var(--ink);
    color: var(--paper);
    border-bottom: 5px solid var(--sun);
  }
  .quote-sample > span {
    color: var(--sun);
  }
  .quote-sample h2 {
    margin: 0.55rem 0 1rem;
  }
  .quote-sample ol {
    list-style: decimal-leading-zero;
    padding-left: 2rem;
  }
  .quote-sample li {
    padding: 0.5rem 0 0.5rem 0.3rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #ffffff42;
  }
  .quote-sample li::marker {
    font: 500 0.8rem var(--mono);
    color: var(--sun);
  }
  .product-index {
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
  }
  .product-index dt {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    padding-top: 0.65rem;
    font-weight: 650;
  }
  .product-index dd {
    margin: 0.2rem 0 1rem;
  }
</style>
